 "rules": {
  "E85-R1_seen": "each main kind (F32, I8, F16): the ROI amplitude's sign-flip p < 0.001 and its transfer phase (lag behind the board power) in (0, 180) degrees: warming that follows the kind",
  "E85-R2_heat_follows_watts": "each main kind: R = |H_kind| / Href(t_kind) equals 1 within max(3 SE_R, 0.10), where H_kind = the kind's camera fundamental over its own board fundamental (mK/W), Href(t) the reference line at the kind block's mid-time, and SE_R the quadrature of the kind's jackknife SE of |H| and the line's SE at t, both divided by Href(t)",
  "E85-R3_pooled": "the inverse-variance mean of the three main kinds' R equals 1 within max(3 SE, 0.05)",
  "E85-R4_same_lag": "each main kind's transfer phase equals the reference line's phase within max(3 SE, 15 degrees), SE = the kind's jackknife phase SE and the line's phase SE in quadrature",
  "E85-R5_near_null": "E85-SP90 (no detection required): its ROI amplitude projected on the reference line's camera direction equals Href(t) x its own board fundamental projected on the reference power direction, within 3 SE (its own SE along that direction)",
  "E85-R6_electrical": "each kind's measured board step (arm A's steady median minus arm B's, mean over analysed laps) inside its predicted band; each reference block's inside +-10% of the earlier 192-minion mean; scored per block",
  "E85-R7_reference_line": "the three reference blocks' |H| lie on a weighted straight line in time: worst residual <= 3 SE (E73's R2); with fewer than three references it is not scored and R2-R5 use the line through what there is",
  "E85-R8_hold": "every block: >= 95% of the 10 Hz samples from 1.5 s after each analysed launch's start to its end read >= 790 MHz, and the block's die mean is below 65 C (E73's R6); the per-launch idle-reset dips are counted and reported with no verdict",
  "E85-R9_absolute": "each main kind's ROI amplitude inside its frozen band [H_lo x 0.8, H_hi x 1.2] x its predicted fundamental, H_lo..H_hi = the six earlier 192-minion transfers: E63's mK per W, not drift-corrected"
 },
